# Topic permissions for the cloud-profile broker (backend/mosquitto/mosquitto.tls.conf).
# PURPOSE: Least privilege per identity. The "user" below is the CN of the client certificate (tools/pki.sh), not a password login.
# HOW: One stanza per identity; no "#" grants anywhere. Topics: ehg/<node>/pkt = packets, ehg/_gw/<gateway>/status = online/offline.
#   A gateway can publish packets and its OWN status only. Readers cannot publish. To add a gateway: tools/pki.sh client ehg-gw-02,
#   then copy the ehg-gw-01 stanza with the new name (both lines). Mosquitto re-reads this file on SIGHUP or restart.
# KNOWN LIMIT: "ehg/+/pkt" lets a gateway publish packets for ANY node id. The fix exists: tools/gen_acl.py writes an ACL with the node list per gateway
#   (deploy/acl/gateways.json); the cloud compose file uses it when EHG_ACL_FILE points at the result. This file stays the simple default for the laptop.
# ROLE IN THESIS: Access control on the gateway-to-broker boundary (docs/decisions/0008-mqtt-mtls-and-topic-acls.md).
# BEFORE -> AFTER: Before: anyone could publish or read everything. After: see the stanzas.

user ehg-gw-01
topic write ehg/+/pkt
topic write ehg/_gw/ehg-gw-01/status

user ehg-bridge
topic read ehg/+/pkt
topic read ehg/_gw/+/status

user ehg-ingest
topic read ehg/+/pkt

user ehg-viewer
topic read ehg/+/pkt

user ehg-exporter
topic read $SYS/broker/clients/connected
topic read $SYS/broker/clients/total
topic read $SYS/broker/messages/received
topic read $SYS/broker/messages/sent
topic read $SYS/broker/bytes/received
topic read $SYS/broker/bytes/sent
topic read $SYS/broker/publish/messages/dropped
topic read $SYS/broker/store/messages/count
topic read $SYS/broker/uptime

# The phone gateway (ios/EHGGateway), pinned to the one board it serves (docs/ios-gateway.md).
user ehg-ios-01
topic write ehg/EHG-93C0/pkt
topic write ehg/_gw/ehg-ios-01/status
